  "description": "Inner-state cues (#172, FR-TURN-3, NFR-PRIV-1): a sentence that asserts what a character thinks or feels ('he secretly thought she looked sad'). A cue word whose subject is another character than the viewpoint's, in a sentence whose content matches that character's private thoughts or beliefs, is a think_leak. Verbs of thought and feeling, adverb cues and cognition verbs; every inflection is listed (no stemmer). An observable action expressing a state (a sympathetic glance) carries no cue.",
